# The message-authentication keys the datasource paths sign with, one per purpose.
#
# They used to be derived from CODEFLY_INTERNAL_TOKEN, the cell-wide perimeter
# credential every service and composed module holds. Two things were wrong with
# that, and neither is visible from either end: every holder of the perimeter
# credential could compute these keys and forge what they authenticate, and
# ROTATING the perimeter credential silently invalidated every outstanding ticket
# and link state — a rotation whose blast radius nothing documented.
#
# A key per purpose, delivered rather than derived, so rotating one rotates one
# thing. Unset leaves the purpose it serves unavailable rather than falling back to
# a derivation: a key reachable from a credential thirteen workloads hold is not a
# key, and a silent fallback would make the fix conditional on nobody forgetting.

# Signs the opaque content tickets a change-set job carries in place of an
# oversized blob. The same value must be present wherever a ticket is redeemed.
DATASOURCE_CONTENT_TICKET_KEY=local-dev-only-replace-me

# Signs the account-link state that carries a person through a provider's sign-in
# and back. Domain-separated from the ticket key above, so neither token can pass
# for the other.
DATASOURCE_ACCOUNT_LINK_KEY=local-dev-only-replace-me
